<title>USA: Illinois winter wheat improves during March.</title>
<headline>Illinois winter wheat improves during March.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois soft red winter wheat improved this past month to 14 percent rated excellent, 63 percent good, 19 fair, two poor and two very poor, as of Sunday, said an Illinois Agricultural Statistics Service report Monday.</p>
<p>Oats planting was under way and as of Sunday, 17 percent of the acreage was planted versus 10 percent a year ago and the 17-percent average.</p>
<p>Sufficient hay was available but some reporters said there may be shortages. Pastures were beginning to green up.</p>
<p>Recent mild weather improved conditions for livestock.</p>
<p>Statewide topsoil moisture was rated 25 percent surplus, 70 percent adequate and five percent short.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
